9c34e-cddd-4d9e-b0aa-6ee4bb642137"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"4e44f93c539e7caa7f17760fcb4eda0703e3b83fb6501fe74608c11f846a0636","event_uuid":"a1e67822-5681-42f8-88ea-30fda686aba5","position":{"commit_sha":"747953590902b5f4eda0f644d25419cd7c06e7fa","position":"1788948795841880001-a1e67822-5681-42f8-88ea-30fda686aba5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"089fb07791475f645c60de60dc29a39704b07f658eacd065386eff520ac9ec2e","event_uuid":"635d9aad-b6f9-4e83-b5cc-3b8e1bc832a6","position":{"commit_sha":"07290dec346a92033c36ecbe6563a5a8e3c5cad6","position":"1788948835952593001-635d9aad-b6f9-4e83-b5cc-3b8e1bc832a6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6ce8aa66b967e9c1c2c0b7ba3072a6aca6e36aa487317fb75999c29b239a6b67","event_uuid":"70822fec-01b0-4c5e-ad03-47028b951dbe","position":{"commit_sha":"cc61cd7cb48d3c162b7e56f61393546dab0dc212","position":"1788948863246014001-70822fec-01b0-4c5e-ad03-47028b951dbe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA/design note: the defect is host-level aggregate resource use, not an individual failing test. I chose candidate (c), minimal both: a portable Makefile-side Python runner registers active full-suite runs in the git common dir, prunes stale pid records, and computes an effective xdist worker count from requested workers, available RAM (4 GiB/worker budget), CPU count, and active full-suite run count. It does not globally serialize development: multiple suites can still run, but each degrades its worker count; low-memory kills remain classified as environmental with serial fallback guidance. I rejected a pure semaphore because it risks queueing/starving agents or serializing full suites outright, and rejected memory-only autoscaling because simultaneous starts can all observe the same free-memory snapshot.","timestamp":1788924481640245001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verification note: full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 completed lint/typecheck and most of the test suite, then hit an existing xdist-sensitive failure in tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py::test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone (asserted missing 'was re-cloned by another container'). The failed test passed immediately in isolation (1 passed in 211.54s), matching prior transient evidence on ticket 7680-85c7-af0d-416f. Created linked follow-up stellar-sane-hawk (b1a3-3e62-f1ff-4748) for that separate flake. Goldeneye-specific targeted tests, lint, typecheck, mechanism ratchet, and guarded runner smoke all pass.","timestamp":1788937043561357001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence: Gerrit 2886 merged at 2e7df98a6de78ba43e0f9ad2d5d94d26b294b554 with LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1 (GitHub run 34335510153). RED was tests/unit/test_pytest_resource_guard.py::test_memory_pressure_reduces_requested_workers failing before scripts/run_default_tests.py existed. Final local verification: targeted resource-guard tests passed (8 passed), make lint passed, make typecheck passed, mechanism ratchet passed with lock marker for ba95-a378-62a5-422c, and make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 passed with GIT_CONFIG_* unset.","timestamp":1788948795841880001}],"created_at":1788913011517224001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"533ec328-8d1b-4a92-be9e-eac287bc97c7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2019-e9ed-0eaa-4a15"},{"link_uuid":"f7241c8c-8d88-4e69-8ba2-dba18e529951","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2ad7-fc8f-427b-485c"},{"link_uuid":"1389c34e-cddd-4d9e-b0aa-6ee4bb642137","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"202b-2040-2e76-4506"},{"link_uuid":"70822fec-01b0-4c5e-ad03-47028b951dbe","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e1f4-9349-9024-40fd"}],"description":"## Observation\nA gating run in one session was killed by low memory (not a test failure). Investigation found three worktrees concurrently running full pytest-xdist suites (bug-lowcost-git-subprocess-timeout, fix-crane-fixture, plus the reporting session). Three concurrent suites on one host exhausted memory. Confirmed environmental cause: host memory contention, remedy applied was halving workers; fallback is serial. This is the same failure class as the 2026-09-06 host memory-exhaustion incident.\n\n## Problem\nmake verify / make test default to PYTEST_WORKERS=4 (often raised to 8) per invocation, with no cross-session coordination. N parallel agent sessions => N*workers pytest processes, unbounded aggregate memory. Each agent behaves correctly locally; the host-level aggregate is the defect. Also noted: pgrep -f pytest matches ALL sessions' workers (text is not identity), so naive post-kill sweeps would kill other sessions' work — cleanup guidance must stay worktree-scoped.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A mechanism bounds aggregate test-suite resource use across concurrent sessions on one host (e.g. cooperative host-wide concurrency cap for full-suite runs, worker autoscaling from available memory, or documented+enforced stagger protocol). Mechanism-ratchet: justify any new lock/env_var with a mechanism-ok marker referencing this ticket.\n- [x] Solution preserves parallel multi-agent development (serializing all verifies outright is unacceptable friction).\n- [x] A killed-by-OOM run is distinguishable from a test failure in guidance/output so agents apply the environmental-fault remedy instead of retrying blind or root-causing a phantom flake.\n- [x] AGENTS.md/docs updated: worktree-scoped process cleanup only (never pgrep -f pytest sweeps); reduced-worker/serial fallback protocol on memory kill.\n- [x] Regression evidence for the chosen mechanism.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2019-e9ed-0eaa-4a15"],["relates_to","202b-2040-2e76-4506"],["relates_to","2ad7-fc8f-427b-485c"],["relates_to","e1f4-9349-9024-40fd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2ce09e32-b44a-4202-b298-0c979f287832","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ba95-a378-62a5-422c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Host memory exhaustion: concurrent agents each run fully parallelized pytest suites","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2ce09e32-b44a-4202-b298-0c979f287832","7b712b59-d9b0-42fe-9cb0-067dd278b7dd","175e9b17-145f-4283-a8d3-0acb99b7eb12","b